---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { person, profiles, listedProfiles } from '../site';

const products = [
  { name: 'BumpSync', href: '/work/bumpsync/', line: 'a pregnancy app for both parents. Couples who connect are 9× more likely to still be using it a month later, so version 2 was rebuilt around getting the second parent in.' },
  { name: 'HushSync', href: '/#hushsync', line: 'hum a lullaby and get back a finished song, with each AI model doing the job it’s best at.' },
  { name: 'LittleSpots', href: '/#littlespots', line: 'where to eat out with a baby. 6,725 venues across Greater Manchester, with AI guesses labelled as guesses until an owner confirms them.' },
  { name: 'Mavropost', href: '/#mavropost', line: 'an AI marketing team that can’t post without a person approving it. It runs BumpSync’s Instagram.' },
];
---
<Base
  title="About"
  fullTitle="Adam Bell, Product Manager in Manchester | AGB Labs"
  description="Adam Bell is a product manager in Manchester: Product Owner for car finance at cinch, formerly Head of Product at Housemates, and builder of four products with AI."
  ogType="profile"
  schema={{
    '@type': 'ProfilePage',
    mainEntity: { '@id': person.id },
    url: 'https://agb-labs.com/about/',
  }}
>
  <article class="wrap about">
    <h1>Adam Bell</h1>
    <p class="lede">Product manager in Manchester. Regulated fintech by day, my own products the rest of the time.</p>
    <ul class="facts" role="list">
      <li><b>Now</b><span>Product Owner, car finance at cinch</span></li>
      <li><b>Before</b><span>Head of Product at Housemates, a student housing marketplace</span></li>
      <li><b>Side</b><span>AGB Labs: four products, built solo with AI</span></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="prose story">
      <h2>Product manager, day job and side projects</h2>
      <p>
        I’m Product Owner for car finance at cinch, which means working on a regulated fintech product.
        Before that I was Head of Product at Housemates, a marketplace for student housing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside work I run AGB Labs, where I decide what to build and then build it. AI coding agents do
        most of the typing; I make the product calls, read the numbers and decide what ships. It’s the
        same job as my day job, with a much shorter loop between a decision and seeing whether it was right.
      </p>

      <h2>What I’ve built</h2>
      <ul>
        {products.map((p) => <li><a href={p.href}>{p.name}</a>: <span set:html={p.line} /></li>)}
      </ul>
      <p>
        Every one can be tried on the <a href="/#products">home page</a>. <a href="/how-i-build/">How I build</a> covers
        the platform behind them: coding agents on a server that I direct from my phone.
      </p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Start with the bet.</strong> Each product begins with one decision about what will make people come back, and the build follows from it.</li>
        <li><strong>Let the numbers change the plan.</strong> BumpSync’s retention data is why its second version looks the way it does.</li>
        <li><strong>Keep AI honest.</strong> If AI guessed something, the product says so, and a person approves anything that goes out in public.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="contact">
      <a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@agb-labs.com">Email me</a>
      {listedProfiles.map((p) => <a class="btn ghost" href={p.url} rel="me noopener">{p.label}</a>)}
      <span class="muted">CV on request.</span>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about { padding-top: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 5rem); }
  .lede { font-size: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--muted); max-width: 36ch; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .facts { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 2.5rem 0 0; display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; max-width: 40rem; }
  .facts li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 5rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; background: var(--surface); border-radius: 16px; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; }
  .facts b { font-family: var(--display); }
  .story { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .story h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .contact { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 48px; padding: 0 1.4rem; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--ink); color: var(--bg); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .btn.ghost { background: var(--surface); color: var(--ink); }
</style>
